! Cisco IOS DHCPv6 clients ('ipv6 address dhcp') wait for a Router Advertisement with the
! Managed flag set before they start a stateful DHCPv6 exchange. r1 is the on-link router
! for the v6 client here -- Kea sits behind the relay, several hops away, so its own RA
! (if any) is link-local and can't reach past the relay. Set the flags on every
! DHCPv6-relaying interface.
{% for intf in interfaces if intf.dhcp.relay.ipv6 is defined %}
interface {{ intf.ifname }}
 ipv6 nd managed-config-flag
 ipv6 nd other-config-flag
!
{% endfor %}
